// t_36492ad8 commit 1.  THE REFERENCE RESOLVES A CALL AGAINST THE
// DECLARATIONS VISIBLE AT THAT CALL.  Our frontend is two-pass, so before
// this every declaration in the unit was visible from everywhere.  Measured
// against sce-cgc 475, sce_fp_rsx.  No defaults appear in any of these - the
// rule is observable without them.
//
// CONTROL: the same call with a prior prototype is ACCEPTED.  Without this
// row a compiler that refused every forward call - prototype or not - would
// satisfy the refusal row above for the wrong reason.

float4 helper(float4 c);
float4 main(float4 t : TEXCOORD0) : COLOR { return helper(t); }
float4 helper(float4 c) { return c * 2.0; }
